WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.600
The future of the Marvel Cinematic Universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:08.120
is in jeopardy with Jonathan Majors' guilty&nbsp;
verdict. So what's the MCU to do with Kang?

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.640
Jonathan Majors has been at the center&nbsp;
of the news cycle for some time now for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:17.680
alarming reasons. Multiple allegations of abuse,&nbsp;
his public relations team cutting ties with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.640
and news of him being dropped from various&nbsp;
projects have taken him from a Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:26.520
rising star to someone who's virtually&nbsp;
untouchable. On December 18, the Marvel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.723
actor was found guilty of harassment&nbsp;
and assault in the third degree. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.723 --> 00:00:35.280
Disney has announced that Majors will no&nbsp;
longer star in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.760
"We just crossed… the threshold."

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.160
No other background details have been&nbsp;
announced as of the making of this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.960
but the Hollywood Reporter noted&nbsp;
that Marvel Studios will still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.760
be moving forward with the upcoming&nbsp;
"Avengers: The Kang Dynasty" film.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.240
In November 2023, Marvel veteran writer&nbsp;
Michael Waldron (who worked on two seasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.760
of "Loki" and "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse&nbsp;
of Madness") came aboard the film — suggesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.600
that a recast (and rethinking of the film's&nbsp;
plot) has been in the works for some time.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:09.440
Majors made his debut as a Kang variant, known&nbsp;
as He Who Remains, on the Disney+ series "Loki."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.680
He returned to the MCU in"Ant-Man and the Wasp:&nbsp;
Quantumania," portraying a more vicious version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:19.280
of Kang that rules the Quantum Realm. In the&nbsp;
"Ant-Man" film's storyline, he plays several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.240
other Kang variants, such as Rama-Tut and&nbsp;
Immortus. Naturally, many have already begun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.120
to ask the big question, where does Marvel&nbsp;
Studios go from here with the Kang character?

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.000
Throughout the MCU's Phase Four and Phase&nbsp;
Five, fans have gotten well-acquainted with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.280
the multiverse. Various forms of Kang have&nbsp;
been depicted as masters of the multiverse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.800
capable of traversing it, bending it&nbsp;
to their will, and working together to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.400
take out anyone against them. This is why he&nbsp;
and his variants have been positioned as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:50.880
Thanos-level threats of the Multiverse Saga,&nbsp;
which encompasses Phases Four, Five, and Six.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.520
Though the folks at Marvel Studios likely could&nbsp;
find a way to write Kang out of the franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:00.080
in favor of another overarching villain, it&nbsp;
arguably wouldn't be the right move. Fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.200
know about the Jonathan Majors situation and&nbsp;
remember how hard Kang was publicly pushed as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:10.600
the MCU's next big bad. All of that information&nbsp;
would loom large over an abruptly Kang-free MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:15.280
likely to the detriment of the franchise. Since&nbsp;
the character seems so essential to the MCU's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:20.600
immediate future, it looks like there's&nbsp;
only one viable way forward: recast Kang.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:24.960
On paper, recasting Kang might seem like&nbsp;
a bad idea. He's a major antagonist who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.160
has shown his face multiple times in the&nbsp;
MCU. So how could Marvel Studios bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.600
the character back with a new actor? Well,&nbsp;
in terms of the current multiversal story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.640
it makes sense for Kang variants to have different&nbsp;
faces. For instance, just look at "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:42.240
No Way Home," where Tom Holland, Tobey Maguire,&nbsp;
and Andrew Garfield all played different versions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:47.360
of Peter Parker. Some different Kangs even appear&nbsp;
in "Quantumania's" brief post-credits scene.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:52.600
Yes, variants can have differing faces in the MCU,&nbsp;
but there's behind-the-scenes precedent too. Since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:57.320
the earliest days of the MCU, actors have been&nbsp;
swapped out in favor of new ones. One of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:02.880
notable examples being Don Cheadle taking over&nbsp;
for Terrence Howard as James "War Machine" Rhodes.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.360
"Next time, baby."

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.640
"Look, it's me, I'm here, deal with it."

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.080
Then there's Mark Ruffalo becoming Hulk&nbsp;
following Edward Norton's departure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:15.200
and Kathryn Newton replacing Emma Fuhrmann&nbsp;
as Cassie Lang. Even Thanos went from Damion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:20.080
Poitier to Josh Brolin, proving there's&nbsp;
no role too big to recast in the MCU.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.320
Regardless, there are so many ways Marvel&nbsp;
Studios could handle the future of Kang the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:30.000
Conqueror in the MCU. Given how meticulous Marvel&nbsp;
Studios head Kevin Feige is with everything else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.386
though, it stands to reason he and his team&nbsp;
already have a multiversal plan in the works.

